{"id":"u-9d8b7f39-d117-4020-b696-52e7479149eb","src":"community","title":"BASI6 Plan: 6 Weeks to Elite Fitness","author":"Mithosphere","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/p6rS7Z-basi6-plan-6-weeks-to-elite-fitness","desc":"Basi6 is a six-week boot camp to prepare you for T Nation apex training programs.\n\nBLOCK 1 (3 Weeks)\nDay 1 – Strength-Skill\nDay 2 – Strength Endurance\nDay 3 – Power\nDay 4 – Hypertrophy\nBLOCK 2 (3 Weeks)\nDay 1 – Strength\nDay 2 – Strength Endurance\nDay 3 – Power\nDay 4 – Hypertrophy\n\nWeek Schedule\nIt’s best to train on the following Mon/Wed/Fri/Sat schedule:\n\nMon Day-1 Workout\nTue\tOff\nWed Day-2 Workout\nThu\tOff\nFri Day-3 Workout\nSat Day-4 Workout\nSun\tOff\n\nRepetition Style Guide\n- Normal: Do the concentric as fast as possible. You’ll get less explosive as fatigue sets in, but keep trying to accelerate. Do the eccentric in roughly 3 seconds.\n- Normal 5/1: Do the concentric as fast as possible. You’ll get less explosive as fatigue sets in, but keep trying to accelerate. Do the eccentric in 5 seconds. Hold in the bottom for 1 second.\n- Normal Peak 2: Do the concentric as fast as possible. You’ll get less explosive as fatigue sets in, but keep trying to accelerate. Do the eccentric in roughly 3 seconds. Hold peak contraction for 2 seconds.\n- Rhythmic: Imagine being a piston where the movement speed is relatively rapid and constant. The concentric and eccentric are about the same rate.\n- Sprint: Go as fast/hard as possible for the prescribed duration.\n- Walking: Go at the same speed you would normally walk for carry exercises.\n- Explosive: Do the movement with the intent to be as violently fast as possible.\n\nBlock 2 Day 4 - Hypertrophy Notes:\nWeek 2 Single Rest/Pause\n- Do 8-10 reps close to failure.\n- Rest 15-20 seconds.\n- Do as many reps as possible.\nWeek 3 Double Rest/Pause\n- Do 8-10 reps close to failure.\n- Rest 15-20 seconds.\n- Do as many reps as possible.\n- Rest 15-20 seconds.\n- Do as many reps as possible.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced","Novice"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-23T01:25:38.292Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Strength-Skill","Rest/Conditioning A","Strength Endurance","Rest/Conditioning B","Power","Hypertrophy","Rest/Conditioning C"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":80,"x":5}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":80,"x":5}]},{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":80,"x":5}]},{"n":"Pendlay Row","sets":[{"r":3,"pct":80,"x":5}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Walk","sets":[{"sec":1200,"secHi":3600,"rpe":7}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Split Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Normal Rep Style. Reps per leg."},{"n":"Prowler Push","sets":[{"r":130,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Walking Rep Style. Distance in feet."}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Clean And Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Normal Rep Style."},{"n":"Waiter Walk","sets":[{"r":130,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Walking Rep Style with dumbbells. Distance in feet."}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Normal Rep Style."},{"n":"Kettlebell Swing","sets":[{"sec":60,"rpe":8,"x":2}],"note":"Rhythmic Rep Style."}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Walk","sets":[{"sec":1200,"secHi":3600,"rpe":7}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Vertical Jump","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Explosive Rep Style. Do the first 2 reps at 80% effort and the last 3 reps at 100% effort."},{"n":"Trap Bar Squat","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":50,"x":3}],"note":"Explosive Rep Style. For speed."}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Medicine-Ball Push Press (Overhead Throw)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Explosive Rep Style. 8 to 12-lb medicine-ball."},{"n":"Push Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Explosive Rep Style."}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Broad Jump","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Explosive Rep Style. Do the first 2 reps at 80% effort and the last 3 r